// EXPECT: E0204 for `300`, which does not fit `u8`
// The check has to be contextual (ADR-0016 §1): the literal has no type of its
// own, so only the annotation says what it must fit. Lowering cannot make this
// check, because lowering does not know the target type.
main :: () {
    g: u8 = 300;
}
